From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:16:27 -0400
Subject: spaces: switcher overflow and reorder, the Space sleep timer's tests,
 downloads on the sidebar button

At overflow the inactive chips shrink to dots in their Space colour and grow
back while the pointer rests on the row (docs/features/spaces.md B24-B26);
Move Left / Move Right on the Space menu reorder the switcher through
SpaceModel::MoveSpace, persisted with the Spaces, and Ctrl-N follows (B27,
the keyboard path; the chip drag is a later pass). The download progress ring
and the started animation target the sidebar's bottom-left button, not the
toolbar's (docs/features/toolbar.md T14, backlog S-41).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 2 (R6-18, R6-21) and the model tests for R6-15.
Removable when: Chromium's tab strip hosts a Space switcher and a downloads
button of its own.
